message: "If you use SE-CaCTS or its atlas, please cite it as below."
title: "SE-CaCTS: a copy-number-aware atlas of lineage- and disease-specific super-enhancers in cancer cell lines"
version: v3.0.1
date-released: 2026-10-03
license: MIT
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.23118970
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.23118970
    description: "Concept DOI: every version"
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.23118971
    description: "Release v3.0.1"
repository-code: "https://github.com/thirtysix/SE-CaCTS"
url: "https://thirtysix.github.io/SE-CaCTS/"
authors:
  - family-names: Barker
    given-names: Harlan
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4125-2522"
    affiliation: "University of Oulu"
abstract: >-
  A per-super-enhancer, per-group specificity score (CaCTS for super-enhancers) computed from public H3K27ac
  ChIP-seq of cancer cell lines, corrected for measured copy number, with a label-permutation false discovery
  rate. Release v3.0.1: 2,422 untreated or control experiments on 519 cell lines; 15,324 lineage-specific and
  13,950 disease-specific super-enhancers at FDR <= 0.10, each a super-enhancer in its own group. Includes the
  pipeline code and a static dashboard of the results.
keywords:
  - super-enhancer
  - H3K27ac
  - ChIP-seq
  - copy number
  - cancer cell lines
  - epigenomics
